#EXTM3U
# Internet radio for evo-esp32: copy this folder to the card and the
# stations appear in the library under Radio, in the order written
# here (alphabetical). Each #EXTINF line names the station on the URL
# line below it; tvg-logo="..." is its picture (a URL, or a path on the
# card relative to this file). Add or remove as you like, or put your
# own .m3u or .pls files here.
#
# A selection of UK stations, with a few from further afield, drawn
# from the radio-browser.info and TuneIn directories and checked on
# 20 October 2026 (the BBC's on the 21st): every stream answered,
# every logo decoded. The streams and logos are the broadcasters' own.
# The player decodes MP3, AAC (AAC-LC and HE-AAC), FLAC and Ogg Vorbis
# from the air, as one stream or as HLS (a playlist of short segments
# in MPEG-TS, the way the BBC broadcasts). Where a broadcaster offers
# both a 48k HE-AAC and a 112k MP3 feed (the Bauer brands), the MP3 is
# listed: it sounds no worse and asks less of the board. The BBC's
# stations are listed by their international feeds, 96k HE-AAC, which
# play anywhere; a listener in the UK can change nonuk to uk and
# low_sbr to high_sbr in a BBC URL for the 320k AAC-LC feed.

